      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the \"tired worker\" analogy is pretty clear. \n\none thing though, is there any way to tell if this is just standard accumulated fatigue or if they've actually hit something more systemic? sometimes it feels less like a \"tired worker\" and more like the progress has been actively sabotaged, you know? like they do everything right but the strength just isn't there. is there a way to distinguish between simple physiological fatigue and some kind of deeper, more stubborn stagnation that doesn't respond to a standard deload?",
      "source": "evaluator"
